WEBVTT

s01-proof
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:08.819
On NEAR mainnet, a signed order was rejected 67 s before
it expired, because the owner had already revoked its key.

s02-name
00:00:09.099 --> 00:00:15.328
Bounded Mandate: give an AI agent trading authority
without unrestricted control of your treasury.

s03-problem
00:00:15.608 --> 00:00:21.667
Pausing an agent stops new orders, but does
not itself invalidate orders already signed.

s04-agent
00:00:21.947 --> 00:00:27.216
The agent cannot sign Intents orders.
Its key can only request a proposal.

s05-contract
00:00:27.496 --> 00:00:36.179
A NEAR contract prices each order from the oracle, checks your
limits, then asks NEAR's MPC network to sign it (Chain Signatures).

s06-verifier
00:00:36.459 --> 00:00:42.731
The NEAR Intents verifier checks that key on every
order, so revoking is one owner call that removes it.

s07-run
00:00:43.011 --> 00:00:52.227
Mainnet, fixed proposals, our own filler: an over-limit
order refused; a 1 USDC order signed and filled.

s08-revoke
00:00:52.507 --> 00:00:57.840
A second signed order was held back. The owner
revoked; removal of the key was confirmed.

s09-reject
00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:03.133
The held order was relayed and rejected:
its signing key no longer exists.

s10-recover
00:01:03.413 --> 00:01:06.912
Recovery returned both assets
to the owner's Intents account.

s11-sandbox
00:01:07.192 --> 00:01:14.189
Sandbox, labelled test doubles: 39 scripted
hostile requests refused across five layers.

s12-limits
00:01:14.469 --> 00:01:21.957
Orders executed before confirmed removal stay
executed. Not an audit; no profit promised.

s13-verify
00:01:22.237 --> 00:01:27.549
Check the mainnet proof against the chain: node verify.mjs --mainnet
(make verify is the offline file check). Start at the overview page.
